section layer c events as well as state transitions is:

the event effect for an event is a text if
    the event is a charity registered
    and the charity of the event is a registered charity
    and the date of the event is a date
    and the text is equal to "New active entry created in register"
    otherwise the event is a charity deregistered
    and the charity of the event is a second registered charity
    and the reason of the event is a second text
    and the date of the event is a second date
    and the event is retrospective
        and true is equal to a thing
        otherwise false is equal to the thing
    and true is equal to the thing
        and the text is equal to "Entry moved to historic; registration void from earlier date"
        otherwise the text is equal to "Entry moved to historic"
    otherwise the event is an annual return filed
    and the charity of the event is a third registered charity
    and the year of the event is a number
    and the event was late
        and true is equal to a second thing
        otherwise false is equal to the second thing
    and true is equal to the second thing
        and the text is equal to "Annual return logged with late flag"
        otherwise the text is equal to "Annual return logged"
    otherwise the event is a required steps notice issued
    and the charity of the event is a fourth registered charity
    and the notice id of the event is a third text
    and the deadline of the event is a third date
    and the text is equal to "Notice reference stored under Art 8(3)(k)"
    otherwise the text is equal to "Register updated".

section cross references as well as charity test is:

meets a charity test if
    the charity has charitable purposes
    and the charity provides public benefit
    and the charity has valid constitution
    and the charity has complete financial info.

a charity has charitable purposes if
    it is not the case that
        the purposes of the charity is a list
        and [] is equal to the list.

a charity provides public benefit if
    the charity has identifiable benefit
    and benefit outweighs detriment for the charity
    and it is not the case that unduly restricts beneficiaries for the charity.

a charity has identifiable benefit if
    it is not the case that the public benefit statement of the charity is "".

benefit outweighs detriment for a charity.

% never holds
a charity has valid constitution if
    it is not the case that the constitution of the charity is "".

a charity has complete financial info if
    the amount of the income of the financials of the charity >= 0
    and the amount of the expenditure of the financials of the charity >= 0.

section handling amendments temporal validity is:

a purpose valid at date for a date D if
    advancement_of_animal_welfare is equal to the purpose
    and D >= 2025-01-01
    or it is not the case that advancement_of_animal_welfare is equal to the purpose.

